                <pb facs="0791" n="707" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg707"/>

                <head>No. 326.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Article</hi> 186 <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >of the Mexican Penal Code.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#center">[Handed to Mr. Bayard by Mr. Romero, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" type="received-date" when="1886-07-29">July 29,
                            1886</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Any crimes that may be committed on the territory of a foreign state by a Mexican
                    against Mexicans or against foreigners, or by a foreigner against Mexicans, may
                    be punished in Mexico, in conformity with the laws of the country, under the
                    following provisions: <list>
                        <label>I.</label>
                        <item>That the accused party should be in Mexico, whether of his own free
                            will or by having been extradited.</item>
                        <pb facs="0792" n="708" xml:id="pg708"/>
                        <label>II.</label>
                        <item>That a proper complaint should be made by the legitimate party in case
                            the guilty person should be a foreigner.</item>
                        <label>III.</label>
                        <item>That the accused party should not have been tried in the country where
                            the crime was committed, or, in case he has been tried, that no
                            acquittal, amnesty, or pardon should have been pronounced in the
                            matter.</item>
                        <label>IV.</label>
                        <item>That the violation of which he may be accused should be considered a
                            crime both in the country where it was committed and in Mexico.</item>
                        <label>V.</label>
                        <item>That the crime should be liable, in accordance with the laws of
                            Mexico, to a more severe punishment than that of arrest.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
